sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Student as 🎓 Student
    participant Portal as 💻 Student Portal UI
    participant RegEngine as ⚙️ Registration Service
    participant PrereqService as 🔍 Prerequisite Engine
    participant TimetableService as 📅 Timetable Conflict Validator
    participant DB as 🗄️ PostgreSQL (Prisma)

    Student->>Portal: Accesses Course Registration for Active Semester
    Portal->>RegEngine: GET /api/v1/offerings?semester=current
    RegEngine->>DB: Query open offerings & remaining seats
    DB-->>RegEngine: CourseOfferings List
    RegEngine-->>Portal: Display available courses & sections

    Student->>Portal: Selects course offerings & sections (e.g. CS201-A, MT102-B)
    Portal->>RegEngine: POST /api/v1/lms/enrollments/register { studentId, offeringIds }

    Note over RegEngine, PrereqService: 1. Prerequisite Validation
    RegEngine->>PrereqService: Check CoursePrerequisites for studentId
    PrereqService->>DB: Query past passed Enrollments (grade != F)
    DB-->>PrereqService: Passed courses history
    
    alt Prerequisite Failed (e.g. CS101 not passed)
        PrereqService-->>RegEngine: Error: Prerequisite CS101 required with min grade C
        RegEngine-->>Portal: 422 Unprocessable (Show Prerequisite Error)
        Portal-->>Student: Display error modal with missing prerequisites
    else Prerequisites Cleared
        PrereqService-->>RegEngine: Prerequisite check PASSED
        
        Note over RegEngine, TimetableService: 2. Timetable Slot Conflict Check
        RegEngine->>TimetableService: Check for overlapping TimetableSlots
        TimetableService->>DB: Query scheduled slots for selected offerings
        
        alt Time Conflict Detected (e.g. Mon 09:00 - 10:30 collision)
            TimetableService-->>RegEngine: Error: Slot clash detected
            RegEngine-->>Portal: 409 Conflict (Show Clash Details)
            Portal-->>Student: Highlight overlapping course timings
        else No Conflicts & Capacity Available
            TimetableService-->>RegEngine: Schedule check PASSED
            
            Note over RegEngine, DB: 3. Atomic Enrollment Transaction
            RegEngine->>DB: prisma.$transaction [create Enrollment, increment enrolledCount]
            DB-->>RegEngine: Enrollment records created with status = ENROLLED
            RegEngine-->>Portal: 201 Created { enrolledCourses, creditHoursTotal }
            Portal-->>Student: Show Success Dashboard & Updated Weekly Timetable
        end
    end
